// Typecheck probe for the verifier tests. The production tsconfig.json covers only
// src/, and Vitest transpiles test/ without typechecking it, so a type error in a
// test is invisible to every command this repository runs.
//
// Measured 2026-09-09 on a clean tree: this probe reports 100 diagnostics and the
// standard typecheck reports 0. Appending `const x: number = "s"` to a verifier test
// takes this probe to 101 and leaves the standard typecheck at 0. Note what does NOT
// discriminate: the probe exits 2 either way, because of the diagnostics it already
// reports, so the observable is the diagnostic, not the exit code.
//
// It has no caller ON PURPOSE, and those 100 diagnostics are the reason: that is
// C-215. A gate wired to this config would be red on a healthy tree, and a gate that
// cannot be green is a blocked merge queue, not a guard. The caller lands with the
// commit that closes C-215 -- that is the commit whose green it would certify, and
// it must assert the diagnostic count, not the exit code.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": { "noEmit": true, "rootDir": "." },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts", "test/**/*.ts"]
}
